WEBVTT

00:00.640 --> 00:02.860
I've decided to team up with Fay.

00:02.860 --> 00:04.830
That's excellent news.

00:04.830 --> 00:08.070
You have to work hard to achieve
Clear in the gods' games.

00:08.070 --> 00:10.410
Yup! I'm going to join another game again!

00:10.410 --> 00:11.450
No, you can't.

00:12.070 --> 00:13.030
Why not?!

00:15.470 --> 00:17.870
Fay, have you explained this
to Lady Leshea?

00:17.870 --> 00:19.520
I did.

00:19.520 --> 00:22.760
I told her the two of us alone don't meet
the minimum number for the game.

00:22.760 --> 00:24.800
So, how many people do we need, then?

00:25.210 --> 00:30.510
About that, I'm sure that Ms. Miranda is more
familiar with the specific numbers, right?

00:30.510 --> 00:32.600
I see. That's fair enough.

00:32.600 --> 00:33.850
However, Fay,

00:34.760 --> 00:37.350
do you notice anything about my outfit?

00:37.350 --> 00:40.690
What? Well, it's a gown, right?

00:40.690 --> 00:42.670
Yes, it's a nightgown.

00:42.670 --> 00:46.060
Just when I thought I could
finally sleep after a night shift!

00:46.060 --> 00:49.780
Lack of sleep is the enemy
of every woman's skin!

00:49.780 --> 00:52.240
I-I'm sorry...

00:52.240 --> 00:53.610
The last subordinate who made

00:53.610 --> 00:55.220
- Hey, how many?
- the same mistake before,

00:55.220 --> 00:57.160
had to clean the courtyard
for a month or so!

00:57.160 --> 00:58.450
- Hey, how many?
- That much?!

00:58.450 --> 00:59.290
The crime of disturbing

00:59.290 --> 01:00.360
- a maiden's sleep is a serious one!

01:00.360 --> 01:01.600
- Hey, tell me!
- a maiden's sleep is a serious one!

01:01.600 --> 01:04.600
- How many people?!
- Geez, I know! I know! I understand now!

01:04.600 --> 01:06.600
I'm sorry!

01:35.410 --> 01:43.710
GODS’ GAMES WE PLAY

02:40.530 --> 02:42.400
PLAYER.03: I AM PEARL DIAMOND
Now, Lady Leshea,

02:42.400 --> 02:44.730
PLAYER.03: I AM PEARL DIAMOND
the Arcane Court recommends teams

02:44.730 --> 02:46.650
be composed of 10 people or more.

02:46.650 --> 02:48.110
Why?

02:48.110 --> 02:50.480
According to the last 30 years of data,

02:50.480 --> 02:54.240
the winning rate of challenging gods
with less than 9 people is less than 4%.

02:54.650 --> 02:59.700
But then the win ratio shoots up to 9% with
10 or more people and 11% with 20 people.

03:00.040 --> 03:01.660
But if it's me and Fay...

03:01.660 --> 03:06.360
The best way to snatch victory in gods' game
is to have more people on your team.

03:06.780 --> 03:11.090
There can be one god, versus any number
of people on the human side.

03:11.090 --> 03:15.470
I would rather it be just me and Fay
than have people who don't love games.

03:15.800 --> 03:17.510
Until you have enough people,

03:17.510 --> 03:21.050
you can form alliances with other teams
that don't have enough people.

03:21.430 --> 03:22.680
Right, Fay?

03:23.310 --> 03:24.020
I'm sorry?

03:24.330 --> 03:27.400
I'm asking you to help Lady Leshea
find some suitable apostles for her.

03:27.730 --> 03:29.440
How is that my job?!

03:29.440 --> 03:32.650
It's the court's job
to facilitate that, isn't it?

03:32.650 --> 03:36.350
You guys should find
the right people for you.

03:36.350 --> 03:38.400
Our staff are amateurs.

03:38.400 --> 03:43.240
We can only objectively identify
good apostles based on your report.

03:48.980 --> 03:50.750
Well, I'm going to sleep now.

04:01.680 --> 04:05.520
Hey, you submitted the member recruiting
application earlier, didn't you?

04:05.790 --> 04:08.480
Yes, they'll contact us
if anyone wants to join up.

04:08.480 --> 04:10.720
Then, what are we doing here?

04:13.160 --> 04:16.400
See the clerk at that counter?
That's the Consultation Corner.

04:17.120 --> 04:19.920
All team applications
are handled electronically,

04:20.310 --> 04:22.410
but there are some problems
that can't be solved.

04:22.870 --> 04:25.890
Say, if you have a problem that you
don't want to discuss with your peers,

04:25.890 --> 04:28.080
you might want to have someone
listen to you, right?

04:28.790 --> 04:32.620
Some apostles come in there looking for
a new team, so we keep an eye on them.

04:33.040 --> 04:36.680
Well, while we're waiting here,
let's see what we can find out.

04:36.680 --> 04:39.560
I've got some friends
from a team called 'Blaze.'

04:40.410 --> 04:42.600
It's been a while, Captain Ashlan.

04:42.600 --> 04:45.740
Fay, is that you?!
You finally contacted me!

04:45.740 --> 04:46.350
Huh?

04:46.350 --> 04:51.060
I was surprised at the stream the other day!
I was wondering where you've been!

04:51.060 --> 04:54.070
And you're not affiliated with
any team right now, right?

04:54.070 --> 04:56.640
Yeah. Actually, I was thinking
of joining your team.

04:56.640 --> 04:58.650
Of course we'd love to have you!

04:58.650 --> 05:01.370
If you decide to do so,
I can start the process today.

05:01.370 --> 05:04.640
And I'd like to bring a former god
named Leoleshea with me.

05:04.640 --> 05:06.160
Huh? Hey!

05:08.070 --> 05:09.580
Why are you hanging up?

05:10.370 --> 05:12.330
Is it possible if you join alone?

05:13.250 --> 05:14.790
What's wrong?

05:14.790 --> 05:16.380
You don't know?

05:16.920 --> 05:19.100
About the "Blood-Soaked God" incident?!

05:19.900 --> 05:21.090
What's that?

05:21.610 --> 05:27.930
She's a former god, so if anyone says
a word against it, she refuses to let it go.

05:30.080 --> 05:34.100
There was this one team that was upset
because they lost in one gods' game.

05:34.450 --> 05:35.200
Yes.

05:36.030 --> 05:40.900
They got drunk and said,
"Gods' games are crap!"

05:41.250 --> 05:45.410
Then, by chance,
the Dragon God was walking by...

05:46.180 --> 05:47.620
What happened?

05:47.620 --> 05:48.460
HERE'S WHAT ASHLAN IMAGINES

05:48.460 --> 05:50.920
HERE'S WHAT ASHLAN IMAGINES
The 20 apostles...

05:50.920 --> 05:53.170
HERE'S WHAT ASHLAN IMAGINES
...were sent to the hospital!

05:56.240 --> 05:57.270
Leshea!

05:57.720 --> 06:00.050
It's not my fault!

06:00.050 --> 06:02.590
You're lying!
Why are you talking so funny?

06:02.590 --> 06:06.680
I-I merely gave them
a slight tap on the shoulder.

06:06.680 --> 06:07.890
Leshea.

06:09.250 --> 06:10.840
It wasn't intentional...

06:11.330 --> 06:13.490
I was wrong about holding my force...

06:14.120 --> 06:19.650
She's a very pretty girl,
but I'm sorry, she can't join our team.

06:21.900 --> 06:25.700
If I had to mention something,
I wish her chests were bigger...

06:30.790 --> 06:33.620
Chests come in all different sizes, right?

06:35.570 --> 06:41.340
When I chose this body, I didn't know
about the tastes of human males.

06:41.960 --> 06:42.800
Yes...

06:42.800 --> 06:44.800
Even in ancient magical civilizations,

06:44.800 --> 06:47.330
I was rumored to have modest chests.

06:48.060 --> 06:50.150
I thought I was going to burn the world.

06:50.150 --> 06:51.890
Are you trying to destroy humanity?!

06:51.890 --> 06:54.600
I mean, I'm reasonably
well-endowed, right?

06:56.060 --> 06:58.520
Y-Yes. You're right.

06:59.590 --> 07:00.580
Excellent.

07:05.180 --> 07:07.990
Leshea, can we have a female captain?

07:08.310 --> 07:10.450
What about her chest?
Is hers smaller than mine?

07:10.750 --> 07:12.170
I have no idea!

07:12.870 --> 07:17.420
More importantly, what I'm about to contact
is a team that excels at game analysts.

07:17.710 --> 07:18.820
Analysts?

07:19.290 --> 07:21.840
A staff member who analyzes the game.

07:21.840 --> 07:24.010
It is standard practice for a team

07:24.420 --> 07:26.630
to have an analyst to analyze the tactics

07:26.630 --> 07:30.160
and a coach to guide
the players in the gods' game.

07:32.260 --> 07:34.120
Oh, Captain Yuki?

07:34.120 --> 07:36.210
Hey Fay, what's up?

07:36.210 --> 07:39.440
Is your team looking
for members right now?

07:39.440 --> 07:42.760
Are you starting to take
an interest in Black Rose?

07:42.760 --> 07:47.150
I'm warning you, there are a lot of apostles
who want to join our team but can't.

07:47.470 --> 07:48.360
What about me?

07:48.360 --> 07:52.080
I'll get you a seat right now.
You're welcome here.

07:52.080 --> 07:54.540
Oh, then, can I invite one more person?

07:54.840 --> 07:58.000
A recommendation from you?
Sure. But who is it?

07:58.000 --> 08:00.460
She's a former god named Leoleshea.

08:00.740 --> 08:01.580
Wha...

08:03.640 --> 08:04.590
Captain Yuki?

08:10.760 --> 08:14.680
She screamed. You're doing
something else, aren't you?

08:15.030 --> 08:18.350
Y-Y-You're wrong!
I didn't do anything!

08:18.350 --> 08:22.310
You're the type of person who says
things when you're in trouble!

08:22.310 --> 08:28.530
B-But I'm not in trouble
or anything at all...

08:28.530 --> 08:30.200
You liar!

08:30.200 --> 08:33.160
I know you're in trouble when you
start talking in your sketchiest,

08:33.160 --> 08:34.830
I'm-a-god tone of voice!

08:35.710 --> 08:37.710
O-Okay, fine.

08:39.100 --> 08:42.900
Well, I have had nothing to do
for the past six months,

08:42.900 --> 08:47.350
so I decided to practice battle games
with humans in the underground coliseum.

08:47.350 --> 08:48.200
And?

08:48.680 --> 08:52.970
The first person I fought
was named Yuki.

08:52.970 --> 08:55.310
I still don't know how to handle
my power back then...

08:55.310 --> 08:56.930
You traumatized Captain Yuki?!

08:56.930 --> 08:59.390
I-I went to visit her in the hospital!

08:59.390 --> 09:01.370
Oh, did you? And?

09:02.490 --> 09:04.790
She screamed and passed out.

09:04.790 --> 09:07.320
What have you done
to further traumatize her?!

09:07.320 --> 09:11.950
It was called the incident of
"Killed by God Twice."

09:11.950 --> 09:13.410
As if I care!

09:15.660 --> 09:19.410
I guess it's going to be tough
getting a current team to take us.

09:20.670 --> 09:25.000
I'm sorry. I wish I got
to know humans better.

09:25.510 --> 09:28.090
Don't worry, I know.

09:28.690 --> 09:31.340
Leshea just wants to play with humans.

09:32.180 --> 09:36.600
That's why she's been reading so much
about humans, trying to understand them.

09:37.610 --> 09:43.110
Well, sometimes the references are
too old and the language is not right.

09:44.450 --> 09:48.610
If we can't get onto a current team,
we can start finding people.

09:49.090 --> 09:52.750
Not just making up the numbers, but friends
that understand each other through games.

09:54.740 --> 09:59.410
And it would be nice to have some useful
ability that'll be useful in the gods' game.

10:00.140 --> 10:01.330
For example, telepo—

10:10.010 --> 10:13.010
GODS’ GAMES WE PLAY

10:17.080 --> 10:18.310
Teleporter?!

10:21.020 --> 10:22.460
Do you know her, Fay?

10:22.850 --> 10:23.600
No...

10:27.060 --> 10:30.030
She probably just came
from upstairs, right?

10:30.340 --> 10:34.640
If so, that's great. There must be
quite a bit of transition distance.

10:35.260 --> 10:37.370
Is she looking for a team, too?

10:37.370 --> 10:41.570
I don't know. Since the teleportation
ability is quite useful and helpful,

10:41.570 --> 10:45.070
I'm sure she'll be recruited
by some teams soon.

10:53.120 --> 10:56.350
I'm Pearl Diamond! I hereby submit
my resignation as of today!

10:56.350 --> 10:57.080
Resignation?!

10:57.080 --> 10:58.930
Stop right there!

11:03.200 --> 11:05.230
It seems I did a good job.

11:05.230 --> 11:08.060
W-W-What's about it?!

11:08.060 --> 11:10.270
What's with that fire earlier?!

11:10.270 --> 11:11.980
Huh? Wait...

11:16.110 --> 11:21.570
You two look startingly similar
to the Dragon God and the big rookie, Fay.

11:21.570 --> 11:23.360
That's us, though.

11:23.360 --> 11:27.190
I'm sorry! I'll withdraw right now!

11:27.190 --> 11:29.130
You don't need to apologize!

11:30.130 --> 11:31.250
Calm down!

11:31.710 --> 11:34.090
We're actually here
to stop you from retiring!

11:35.240 --> 11:38.270
Actually, we're just looking for
teammates to play games.

11:38.270 --> 11:39.640
No, I can't.

11:39.640 --> 11:41.080
At least hear us out.

11:41.080 --> 11:43.030
I'm sorry!

11:43.030 --> 11:48.400
O-Okay! I'll buy you a parfait! Can you
give us some time to talk while you—

11:48.400 --> 11:49.360
Sure.

11:50.460 --> 11:51.480
You mean it?!

11:57.110 --> 11:59.560
I'm Pearl Diamond, 16 years old.

11:59.560 --> 12:02.410
I have one win and one loss
in gods' games.

12:04.790 --> 12:06.250
What's up?

12:06.250 --> 12:10.710
It's delicious.
My cheeks are about to fall off!

12:11.110 --> 12:12.340
Oh, I see...

12:13.180 --> 12:16.520
That's right, that ability before
was teleportation, right?

12:16.960 --> 12:18.460
It's "The Wandering."

12:18.460 --> 12:19.080
Huh?

12:19.080 --> 12:24.180
That's what I named my Arise.
Teleporter just sounds boring.

12:24.180 --> 12:25.190
I see...

12:25.900 --> 12:27.130
One win...

12:27.130 --> 12:29.020
She's only an apostle of rank 1,

12:29.020 --> 12:32.690
and that's such a powerful ability that
she jumped across one floor of a building.

12:33.220 --> 12:35.520
And she wants to retire
just because of one loss?

12:39.550 --> 12:42.950
For the apostles, gods' games
are more like work.

12:42.950 --> 12:47.120
Like professional athletes,
they work hard every day.

12:47.470 --> 12:49.010
Apostles are regarded as heroes,

12:49.010 --> 12:52.540
and when they walk the streets,
they are cheered and asked for autographs.

12:52.840 --> 12:54.950
In other words,
they are admired by the people.

12:55.720 --> 12:58.500
However, that will end
if they lose three times.

12:58.880 --> 13:03.510
That is why everyone is desperately
trying to win the game. But why?

13:10.760 --> 13:13.270
I'm sorry, I'm enjoying it all for myself.

13:13.270 --> 13:14.610
No, it's fi—

13:14.610 --> 13:16.400
How much did you eat?!

13:16.780 --> 13:21.360
35 cups. She's been eating
while you've been in a daze.

13:21.360 --> 13:22.660
Ugh...

13:24.680 --> 13:28.000
By the way, I checked your loss data.

13:29.980 --> 13:31.710
Is this why you retired?

13:32.970 --> 13:35.170
We lost because of my mistake.

13:38.830 --> 13:41.090
Noo!

13:49.970 --> 13:54.580
Switching your position with
the captain wasn't teleportation...

13:54.580 --> 13:56.040
A Shift Change.

13:56.450 --> 13:58.610
So you can use two kinds
of teleportation, huh?

13:58.610 --> 14:02.290
Teleportation is to move a person or object,

14:02.290 --> 14:05.570
and shift change is to swap places,
like the parfaits you just did.

14:07.050 --> 14:11.910
The rule of the game at that time
was to protect the leader.

14:12.450 --> 14:17.170
So the whole team lost, and you were
disgusted with yourself like that.

14:17.170 --> 14:20.760
I was scared at the moment
that I was going to be trampled.

14:21.450 --> 14:24.020
I was so scared that I selflessly
invoked my power.

14:24.680 --> 14:27.950
Maybe you lost because you used
your power in the wrong way,

14:28.530 --> 14:31.980
but didn't you also help
the team with your power?

14:32.950 --> 14:35.440
I didn't live up to their expectations.

14:36.180 --> 14:40.430
Even shift change isn't as universal
a power as everyone says.

14:41.310 --> 14:45.160
I can only use shift change if I touch
something within three minutes,

14:45.160 --> 14:47.870
but I used it at the wrong time.

14:49.530 --> 14:51.480
Because of my mistake,

14:52.000 --> 14:56.000
my teammates retired
after they'd lost three times.

14:58.180 --> 15:02.380
I'm really scared...
I'm a total klutz...

15:02.380 --> 15:06.200
And it's thanks to my team
that I have one win...

15:07.300 --> 15:09.140
One win, huh?

15:09.890 --> 15:11.470
Are you taking us gods lightly?

15:12.880 --> 15:17.980
There's no way a team with a klutzy apostle
could win a game against a god.

15:18.420 --> 15:20.050
You said your name was Pearl?

15:20.050 --> 15:21.150
Y-Yes.

15:21.150 --> 15:26.490
It's okay if you make a mistake.
And if we lose, me and Fay won't blame you.

15:27.960 --> 15:30.580
How about it? Let's give it a shot first.

15:32.680 --> 15:36.960
I'm sorry! I've already
made up my mind to retire!

15:36.960 --> 15:38.080
Hey!

15:44.240 --> 15:46.010
Better find someone else, huh?

15:55.230 --> 15:57.640
GAMES ARE MEANT TO BE FUN

15:58.230 --> 16:02.360
GOD SMILES ONLY AT THOSE WHO DISCOVER
MIRACLES ON THEIR OWN

16:03.560 --> 16:04.740
Let's do some investigating.

16:04.740 --> 16:05.830
About what?

16:06.210 --> 16:08.240
Pearl's room number in the girl's dormitory.

16:08.840 --> 16:11.660
I feel like it would be a waste
to let it end this way.

16:11.660 --> 16:13.740
Because her teleport ability
would be so useful?

16:15.180 --> 16:18.870
If she stops now, she'll be afraid
of games for the rest of her life.

16:19.690 --> 16:21.290
That would be sad, right?

16:36.400 --> 16:38.540
What? It's not locked.

16:38.540 --> 16:40.690
Don't tell me she's already
cleaned out her room!

16:42.170 --> 16:43.650
Pearl! Are you there?!

16:44.910 --> 16:46.430
Oh, so you are here.

16:46.820 --> 16:48.070
Wait... Huh?

16:48.070 --> 16:51.030
W-W-Wha...

16:51.950 --> 16:53.740
No way...

16:54.430 --> 16:56.450
I-It's so big...

16:56.780 --> 16:58.970
It's way too big!

16:58.970 --> 17:02.380
This is a catastrophe!

17:02.380 --> 17:04.000
What are you talking about?!

17:05.380 --> 17:08.800
Give me half of your chest meat!

17:11.970 --> 17:16.430
Nooo!

17:17.240 --> 17:19.940
I usually use the warp portal,

17:19.940 --> 17:23.900
so I didn't close it properly,
maybe for half a year.

17:25.360 --> 17:31.730
But thanks to that...
You got a look at my stuff, I mean...

17:31.730 --> 17:34.660
Well, umm...
Sorry.

17:34.660 --> 17:38.490
No, I'm sorry too!
It was my fault!

17:38.490 --> 17:42.190
But you have to take responsibility
and make me happy for the rest of my life!

17:42.190 --> 17:44.140
How much of a responsibility is that?

17:44.140 --> 17:45.790
I'm just kidding.

17:48.730 --> 17:53.370
Actually, I debuted
last year like you, too.

17:53.370 --> 17:59.430
But I admired you so much for
how great you were right off the bat.

18:00.900 --> 18:05.670
That's why I think
I don't belong on your team.

18:06.020 --> 18:07.310
That's not...

18:08.910 --> 18:11.900
I'm just dragging you down.

18:15.320 --> 18:16.160
What are those?

18:16.160 --> 18:18.950
Sweets. Since I'm quitting being an apostle,

18:19.660 --> 18:24.410
I went to apologize to my teammates,
but they didn't accept them.

18:25.050 --> 18:27.160
The captain was out,

18:27.560 --> 18:31.390
but everyone said, "You don't
deserve to meet the captain."

18:33.980 --> 18:39.970
That's right, even if I try to apologize,
it only brings back bad memories.

18:39.970 --> 18:41.930
That is so wrong!

18:41.930 --> 18:43.030
S-Sorry?

18:43.030 --> 18:46.220
You and your teammates
don't understand games!

18:46.220 --> 18:50.950
Whether you win or lose, you're supposed to
have had fun and want to play the game again.

18:50.950 --> 18:52.570
T-That's...

18:52.570 --> 18:55.480
In the gods' games,
it's natural for the gods to win.

18:55.890 --> 18:58.620
It's ridiculous to blame one person
just because you're losing.

18:59.320 --> 19:03.080
T-That's very nice of you to say...

19:06.680 --> 19:10.150
...but it doesn't change the fact
that I'm not good for anything.

19:10.710 --> 19:13.510
You still have the chance
to clear your name, don't you?

19:13.510 --> 19:14.340
What?

19:14.650 --> 19:15.880
Inferno, wasn't it?

19:15.880 --> 19:19.300
You have to go with them when they're
taking on one of the games again.

19:19.300 --> 19:20.260
What?!

19:20.570 --> 19:21.990
Then you can show yourself.

19:21.990 --> 19:24.600
I can't do it!
I could never do it all by myself!

19:24.960 --> 19:27.310
That's why we're going to join with you.

19:27.610 --> 19:28.260
Huh?

19:28.260 --> 19:31.470
The three of us will go
help your former teammates.

19:31.910 --> 19:33.240
You can do that.

19:33.240 --> 19:34.530
B-But...

19:34.820 --> 19:37.990
It's frustrating to end up losing
all the time at a game, isn't it?

19:45.070 --> 19:47.170
It's a loss you'll never forget,

19:47.880 --> 19:51.220
but it's only one loss.
You still have the right to take revenge.

19:51.670 --> 19:54.210
The right to challenge gods again.

19:55.330 --> 19:56.360
I...

19:57.580 --> 19:59.070
We'll go with you just once.

19:59.730 --> 20:01.280
I won't try to stop you after that.

20:03.890 --> 20:09.560
Geez... I've never been scouted
so enthusiastically like this before.

20:10.460 --> 20:11.880
Thank you very much.

20:12.610 --> 20:16.510
I'm Pearl Diamond,
and I'd like to join you.

20:22.530 --> 20:25.540
I-I don't think I can do this!

20:25.540 --> 20:28.080
You've attracted
a little attention, that's all.

20:32.550 --> 20:36.850
You have broken the discipline to say
that today was Inferno dive day,

20:36.850 --> 20:38.980
so you have to win.

20:38.980 --> 20:40.550
Sorry for asking too much.

20:40.850 --> 20:44.040
Well, you guys got the ratings before,
so I'll make an exception.

20:44.470 --> 20:45.440
Pearl.

20:45.440 --> 20:46.270
Yes!

20:46.270 --> 20:49.500
The whole world is watching this battle.

20:49.500 --> 20:50.730
Good luck.

20:56.760 --> 20:59.110
It's a game.
Let's have fun.

20:59.800 --> 21:01.570
Y-Yes.

21:03.120 --> 21:03.970
Let's go.

21:03.970 --> 21:04.910
Right!

21:07.080 --> 21:10.980
Okay, now when you go through the statue
of a giant god, hold your breath...

21:10.980 --> 21:12.000
Let's go.

21:12.280 --> 21:16.420
W-Wait a minute!
I'm not ready yet!

21:18.010 --> 21:20.630
When we fail at a game,
we make up for it with a victory.

21:22.090 --> 21:22.950
Let's go!

21:31.730 --> 21:32.690
Wha...

21:32.690 --> 21:35.650
What is this?!

21:41.380 --> 21:43.030
There's something under the clouds!

21:50.840 --> 21:51.960
This god...

21:52.580 --> 21:56.300
In the past, this was a god
that no one had succeeded in defeating.

21:56.300 --> 21:59.280
This was the god of despair...

22:02.840 --> 22:04.040
...Uroboros!

22:05.020 --> 22:07.570
Perfect! I'll play your game,

22:08.010 --> 22:09.410
no matter what it is!
